Key methodologies include the use of wage data from the New Immigrant Survey, Mexican Migration Project, and Latin American Migration Project to analyze immigrants' experiences and control for selection biases. The study uses these data to compare wage changes at migration with gaps in GDP per worker, providing insights into the contribution of human capital versus physical capital and total factor productivity.

